#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:1
msgid "Release 1.6.1 (2013-10-28)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:3
msgid "This is primarily a bug fix release. Changes of interest are:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:5
msgid ""
"Nix 1.6 accidentally changed the semantics of antiquoted paths in strings, "
"such as `\"${/foo}/bar\"`. This release reverts to the Nix 1.5.3 behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:9
msgid ""
"Previously, Nix optimised expressions such as `\"${expr}\"` to _expr_. Thus "
"it neither checked whether _expr_ could be coerced to a string, nor applied "
"such coercions. This meant that `\"${123}\"` evaluatued to `123`, and `\"${./"
"foo}\"` evaluated to `./foo` (even though `\"${./foo} \"` evaluates to `\"/"
"nix/store/hash-foo \"`). Nix now checks the type of antiquoted expressions "
"and applies coercions."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:16
msgid ""
"Nix now shows the exact position of undefined variables. In particular, "
"undefined variable errors in a `with` previously didn't show _any_ position "
"information, so this makes it a lot easier to fix such errors."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:21
msgid ""
"Undefined variables are now treated consistently. Previously, the `tryEval` "
"function would catch undefined variables inside a `with` but not outside. "
"Now `tryEval` never catches undefined variables."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:25
msgid "Bash completion in `nix-shell` now works correctly."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:27
msgid ""
"Stack traces are less verbose: they no longer show calls to builtin "
"functions and only show a single line for each derivation on the call stack."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.6.1.md:31
msgid ""
"New built-in function: `builtins.typeOf`, which returns the type of its "
"argument as a string."
msgstr ""
